---
interface Props { piece?: string }
const { piece = 'piece' } = Astro.props;
/*
  READ ALOUD. The essay, spoken by the reader's own device.

  Denvil asked on 30 Aug whether the essays could be listened to. This is the
  version that costs nothing and works today: the browser's own speech
  synthesis, which every current phone and desktop has built in. No service, no
  key, no per-essay generation, no audio files to host, and nothing leaves the
  page. It reads whatever is in the article, so it works on every piece ever
  published without anybody doing anything to them.

  What it is not is Denvil's voice, and it should not pretend to be. The
  control says "Listen to this essay" and the small print names the device as
  the reader, so nobody presses play expecting the preacher and gets a robot.
  If he ever records these himself, this component is where that audio would
  go instead, and the button would not have to move.

  Two things it does that a naive implementation gets wrong:

  1. It reads the essay, not the furniture. Pull quotes and big ideas are lifted
     out of his sentences, so reading the page top to bottom says them twice.
     Scripture blocks hold four translations at once, of which three are hidden.
     So the text is gathered from the visible panes and the real paragraphs, in
     document order, and the duplicated display treatments are skipped.

  2. It breaks the text into sentence-sized utterances. Chrome silently stops
     after about fifteen seconds of a single long utterance, which on a
     2,500-word essay means it dies in the first paragraph. Feeding it a queue
     of sentences also makes pause, resume and stop behave.

  It hides itself when the browser has no speech synthesis at all, rather than
  offering a button that does nothing.
*/
---
<div class="ra" data-read-aloud data-ra-idle={`Listen to this ${piece}`} hidden>
  <button type="button" class="ra-btn" data-ra-toggle aria-live="polite">
    <span class="ra-ico" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" focusable="false">
        <path class="ra-play" d="M8 5.5v13l11-6.5z" fill="currentColor" />
        <g class="ra-pause" hidden><rect x="8" y="5.5" width="3.4" height="13" rx="1" fill="currentColor" /><rect x="13.6" y="5.5" width="3.4" height="13" rx="1" fill="currentColor" /></g>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span class="ra-label" data-ra-label>Listen to this {piece}</span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="ra-stop" data-ra-stop hidden>Stop</button>
  <p class="ra-note">Read aloud by your device, not by Denvil.</p>
</div>
